{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And Jacob loved Rachel.</b> He had already set his eyes on her." "<b>I will serve you.</b> The bet has a hatef-qamatz." "<b>Seven years.</b> He should have said a year or two; but it was not in Jacob's mind that they would give him a beautiful wife like Rachel for meager labor, therefore he said seven years." "<b>For Rachel your younger daughter.</b> Who is not esteemed in your eyes like Leah, for she is a shepherdess, and therefore he said 'to be a shepherdess in her stead.' Another interpretation: <b>For Rachel</b> — he said, if I take the birthright, Esau will come back and attack me and say, it was not enough for you that you took my birthright and my blessing, but you also took my wife by force."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:37.441794522Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}